  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 061128\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 AM HST Fri Nov 06 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nEastern Central Pacific (CP95):\nShowers and thunderstorms associated with a trough of low pressure\nlocated several hundred miles to the southeast of the Big Island of\nHawaii continue to show signs of organization. Environmental\nconditions are conducive for additional development, and a tropical\ndepression is expected to develop later today or on Saturday. The\nsystem is forecast to move west-northwestward to westward at 10 to\n15 mph, passing well south of the Hawaiian Islands.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...high...90 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...90 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Adams\nNNNN",
